{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>But if you indeed keep.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): if you keep the commandments of the Torah, the Holy One, blessed be He, will drive the enemies from before you, for on this condition you are entering the land." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> ״אם שמור תשמרון״ — if you keep (שמור) the commandments of the Torah, then ״תשמרון״ — that is, you will be guarded (תהיו נשמרים) from every enemy and every harm. And so the earlier passage began, ״והיה אם שמוע תשמעו״ — if you hear (שמוע) the words of the Torah, then ״תשמעו״ — that is, you will be heard (תהיו נשמעים); and from the implication of the affirmative you infer the negative, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 21:13): ״אוטם אזנו מזעקת דל גם הוא יקרא ולא יענה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:39.145785871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}